=begin
  stash.lic

  Puts things from your containers in your Eddy, the effervescent eddy you
  wear (a portable vault: 250 things, 1700 stones), right where you stand.
  ;unstash gets it all back. Without an Eddy, or for what it won't take
  (full, or too big), it's your vault at your hometown's Carousel instead
  (Crossing: ;go2 8285, through an arch, PULL LEVER, GO DOOR, OPEN VAULT),
  and then it closes the vault and leaves you in the Carousel. Weapons go in
  the Eddy too: ;unstash weapons, at the start of t2's hunt block, puts them
  back where combat-trainer keeps them. ;vault-to-eddy moved the vault's
  things into the Eddy (2026-11-27).

  Usage:
    ;stash crafting        # forging, shaping, enchanting, outfitting and alchemy gear and materials
    ;stash crafting forging    # the same as ;stash forging (shaping, enchanting, outfitting, alchemy too): t2's crafting blocks end with it
    ;stash forging         # just forging gear and materials
    ;stash shaping         # just shaping gear and materials
    ;stash enchanting      # just enchanting gear and materials
    ;stash outfitting      # just outfitting gear and materials
    ;stash alchemy         # just alchemy gear
    ;stash materials       # just the materials, no gear: ingots, ore, lumber, deeds, stacks, stone, beads, cloth...
    ;stash materials forging   # just one discipline's materials (shaping, enchanting, outfitting too)
    ;stash weapons         # the weapons in your yaml's weapon_training, for when you're not hunting
    ;stash extras          # just your extras
    ;stash all             # crafting gear and materials plus your extras
    ;stash add <item>      # add something to your extras (taps it first to check the name)
    ;stash remove <item>   # take something off your extras
    ;stash list            # show your gear, your extras, and what's stashed right now

  Crafting gear is forging_tools, shaping_tools, enchanting_tools,
  outfitting_tools and alchemy_tools from your yaml, plus the books, logbooks
  and supplies in SUPPLIES below. It comes out of your crafting_container,
  one of each.

  Crafting materials are whatever LOOK IN shows in your crafting_container
  and storage_containers that MATERIALS below says a discipline uses: ingots,
  bars and ore for forging, lumber, deeds, bone stacks and stone for shaping,
  beads and metal shards for enchanting, leather, cloth and dyes for
  outfitting, and so on. Every one gets stashed, from whichever container
  it's in. A weapon harness isn't looked in: only weapons are tied to it.
  Sigil-scrolls stay with you, for the next artificing order to use.

  Except coal nuggets: they're thrown out instead (TRASH below), into a bin
  if the room has one or else dropped, or down the vault's garbage chute at
  the vault. remedy and taskmaster buy one whenever none is on hand, and the
  marathon never uses one. The marathon's stock (burlap cloth, rat-pelt
  leather, wool yarn, cotton thread) is stashed like any other material, and
  ;unstash marathon brings it back with the outfitting tools.

  Weapons are the ones named in your yaml's weapon_training. Each comes out
  of wherever your yaml's gear list says it's kept, the way combat-trainer
  gets it: taken off if you wear it, off its harness, out of its sheath or
  container. They go in the Eddy like everything else, or the vault for
  what the Eddy won't take. ;unstash weapons puts them back the way
  combat-trainer does after a hunt (worn again if your standard gear set
  wears it). t2's hunt block runs it before every hunt, and it does nothing
  when no weapons are stashed.

  Extras are your own list, kept in EXTRAS. It starts as codex, textbook and
  contract. Every one of them you're carrying gets stashed, from whichever
  container it's in.

  If the Eddy is full, the rest goes to the vault. If the vault is full too,
  the rest stays where it is. If rent is due, nothing goes to the vault: pay
  at the Carousel desk first (GO DESK, 5,000 Kronars for 30 days).

  What went in is written to STASHED so ;unstash gets back exactly those
  things and puts them back where they came from. Each one is written down
  with where it went (in: eddy, or the vault) and what it's for (forging,
  shaping, enchanting, outfitting, alchemy, weapons or extras), so
  ;unstash forging and the like get back just that. Materials are marked as
  materials: ;unstash crafting and ;unstash forging leave them stashed, and
  ;unstash materials gets them.
=end

# What's stashed right now. Shared with unstash.
STASHED = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'stash.yaml')
# Your extras, changed with ;stash add and ;stash remove
EXTRAS = File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'stash-extras.yaml')
DEFAULT_EXTRAS = %w[codex textbook contract].freeze

# Crafting gear besides each discipline's tools from your yaml
SUPPLIES = {
  'forging' => [
    'weapon.book', # book of journeyman weaponsmithing instructions (since 11/20/2026)
    'forging logbook',
    'oil', # flask of oil
    'flux' # borax flux
  ],
  'shaping' => [
    'shap.book', # book of journeyman shaping instructions (since 11/26/2026)
    'engineering logbook'
  ],
  'enchanting' => [
    'artificing book', # book of apprentice artificing instructions
    'enchanting logbook',
    'fount' # fragile rough mana fount
  ],
  # Bought 11/9/2026
  'outfitting' => [
    'tailoring book', # book of journeyman tailoring instructions (since 11/25/2026)
    'outfitting logbook'
  ],
  # Bought 11/9/2026. remedy.lic gets the book as "remed book".
  'alchemy' => [
    'remed.book', # book of apprentice remedies instructions
    'alchemy logbook'
  ]
}.freeze
# ;stash crafting does all of these
DISCIPLINES = SUPPLIES.keys.freeze

# The sizes ore and metal pieces come in, from Elanthipedia's Mining page
ORE_SIZES = '(?:tiny|small|medium|large|huge|massive|enormous|gargantuan)'

# What each discipline crafts from, matched against the item names LOOK IN
# shows ("huge pewter bar", "heavy wool cloth"). Every match gets stashed,
# except TRASH, which goes down the chute.
MATERIALS = {
  'forging'    => {
    'ingots'     => /\bingot$/i,
    'nuggets'    => /\bnugget$/i,
    'metal bars' => /\bbar$/i,
    # Mined ore: a size, then the metal ("large muracite fragment", "massive
    # quelium lump")
    'metal ore'  => /\b#{ORE_SIZES} \S+ (?:fragment|lump)$/i
  },
  'shaping'    => {
    'lumber'       => /\blumber$/i,
    'lumber deeds' => /\b(?:stick|branch|limb|log) \S+ deed$/i, # log walnut deed; sizes from clean-lumber.lic
    'bone stacks'  => /\bstack$/i,
    'stone deeds'  => /\b(?:pebble|stone|rock|boulder) \S+ deed$/i, # rock quartzite deed, for carving
    # Loose stone, by its size noun: "white mocha stone". Not starstone or
    # runestone, which have no word break before "stone".
    'stones'       => /\b(?:pebble|stone|small rock|large rock|boulder)$/i
  },
  # Not sigil-scrolls: artificing orders use the ones in your bag before buying
  # more, and ;unstash enchanting would leave stashed ones in the vault. They'd
  # been put back by accident since 2026-11-18 (GET's name for one ends in
  # "comprised of broad strokes"); the user asked to keep it so (2026-11-25).
  'enchanting' => {
    # A stone, bone or wood bead is a base for trinkets and foci
    'beads'         => /\bbead$/i,
    # A metal by its size, like forging's ore: "massive selatila shard", a
    # taskmaster reward, which ;stash materials missed (2026-11-10)
    'metal shards'  => /\b#{ORE_SIZES} \S+ shard$/i
  },
  'outfitting' => {
    'leather' => /\bleather$/i,
    # Any fabric: burlap and wool, and the rare ones taskmaster hands out
    # ("fine steelsilk cloth", "thin Imperial weave cloth", "thin titanese
    # cloth", "fine zenganne cloth"), which a list of the plain fabrics missed
    # (2026-11-18). Not a chamois, cleaning or polishing cloth: those are tools.
    'cloth'   => /\A(?!.*\b(?:chamois|cleaning|polishing)\b).*\bcloth$/i,
    'yarn'    => /\byarn$/i,
    'thread'  => /\bthread$/i,
    'dyes'    => /\bdye$/i
  },
  # Herbs stay in your remedy_container
  'alchemy'    => {}
}.freeze

# Materials not worth keeping, which are thrown out instead of stashed (down
# the vault's garbage chute at the vault): remedy and taskmaster buy a coal nugget whenever
# none is on hand, and the marathon never uses one (2026-11-18). Only coal:
# a gold nugget is a keeper.
#
# This used to be WORKING_STOCK, things left with you because the scripts
# use the bag's stock (2026-11-10). The user asked for the marathon's thread,
# yarn, rat-pelt leather and burlap to be stashed instead, with ;unstash
# marathon to bring them back (2026-11-18).
TRASH = ['coal nugget'].freeze
TRASH_PATTERN = /\b(?:#{TRASH.map { |name| Regexp.escape(name) }.join('|')})$/i
# "You drop a steel ingot into the garbage chute.  A flap prevents it from
# falling all the way down until you leave the chamber." (2026-11-10)
CHUTE_DROPPED = [/^You drop .* into the garbage chute/].freeze

# A deed's name is different in GET and in LOOK: what LOOK lists as "log
# lelori deed", GET calls "a deed for a thick lelori log". The check that GET
# took a material (2026-11-18) only knew LOOK's, so it put every lumber deed
# and most stone deeds back (found 2026-11-25).
DEED_FOR = /\Adeed for (?:an?|some) (?:.+ )?(\S+) (\S+)\z/i

# storage_containers that can't hold materials, so aren't looked in
NOT_LOOKED_IN = /\bharness\b/i

# The Eddy, from Fizzlestiks's first look at it (2026-11-27): you PUT things
# in the eddy, and GET and LOOK through its portal ("LOOK IN PORTAL -or LOOK
# IN WATERY PORTAL"). Always "my": LOOK IN PORT at the Strand looked in the
# meeting portal there. GET finds nothing until you LOOK in the portal
# (DRCI's get_item_from_eddy_portal? says so too). The same in unstash and
# vault-to-eddy.
EDDY = 'my eddy'
EDDY_PORTAL = 'my portal'
EDDY_OPENED = [/^You open/, /already open/i].freeze
EDDY_LOOKED = [/^In the .*/, /nothing in there/i].freeze
EDDY_UNREACHABLE = [/^What were you referring to/, /^I could not find/, /^I don't know what you are referring to/,
                    /funnel downward/, /^You can't/, /interfer/i].freeze
# "There isn't any more room in the eddy for that." (dr-scripts' own tests).
# The weight limit's message isn't known yet, so those are guesses.
EDDY_FULL = [/isn't any more room/i, /too heavy/i, /\bweight\b/i, /too many/i, /\bfull\b/i].freeze
# Just this one won't go in ("fit within the eddy container's dimensions")
EDDY_REFUSED = [/^You can't/, /^You must/, /\bfit\b/i, /too (?:big|large|long|wide|tall)/i, /^That's/, /^What were you referring to/].freeze

# Getting in and out of the vault, as Fizzlestiks did it at the Crossing
# Carousel on 2026-11-07 and 11-08. Plain GO ARCH is the platinum arch, which
# the attendant blocks ("Sorry, but access to that arch is restricted."), so
# it isn't tried. The blackwood, ironwood and rosewood arches all work
# ("The Dwarven attendant escorts you through the ironwood arch."). A busy
# booth: 'The attendant steps in front of the blackwood arch.  "Sban is using
# that booth," he says.'
ARCHES = ['go blackwood arch', 'go ironwood arch', 'go rosewood arch'].freeze
ARCH_IN = /escorts you through/
RENT_DUE = /\brent\b/i
ARCH_RESTRICTED = /access to that arch is restricted/
ARCH_BUSY = /is using that booth|blocks|someone|using|Sorry/
LEVER_PULLED = /door pops open/
VAULT_OPENED = [/^The vault opens/, /already open/i].freeze
CHAMBER = /Chamber/
# Where you may be already, as ;trash-sort leaves you. The map doesn't know
# these rooms, so walking to the Carousel from them fails ("DRCT: Unable to
# resolve the current room", 2026-11-22).
CAROUSEL_CHAMBER = /Carousel Chamber/
CAROUSEL_BOOTH = /Carousel Booth/

# bput returns only the matched text, so these match the whole line
GET_SUCCESS = [/^You get .*/, /^You pick up .*/].freeze
PUT_SUCCESS = [/^You put .*/].freeze
TAP_SUCCESS = [/^You tap\s(?!into).*/, /^As you tap .*/, /^You (?:thump|drum) your finger.*/].freeze
NOT_FOUND = [/^What were you referring to/, /^I could not find/, /^I don't know what you are referring to/].freeze
# The vault's full message isn't known yet, so these are guesses
VAULT_FULL = [/no room/i, /isn't any more room/i, /\bfull\b/i, /too many/i, /maximum/i].freeze
# Just this item won't go in
PUT_FAILURE = [/^You can't/, /^You must/, /^Weirdly, you can't/, /is too .* to (fit|hold)/, /to fit in the/].freeze

# "You get a paper-wrapped textbook from inside your grey rucksack."
GET_NAME = /^You (?:get|pick up) (?:a|an|some|the|your) (.+?)(?: from .*)?\.$/
GET_SOURCE = /from inside your (.+?)\.$/
# "You tap some bundling rope inside your grey rucksack." or "... that you are holding."
TAP_NAME = /^You tap (?:a|an|some|the|your) (.+?)(?: inside your (.+?)| that you are (\w+))?\.$/

def load_yaml(path, default)
  File.exist?(path) ? YAML.safe_load(File.read(path)) || default : default
end

def save_yaml(path, data)
  FileUtils.mkdir_p(File.dirname(path))
  File.write(path, data.to_yaml)
end

def load_extras
  load_yaml(EXTRAS, DEFAULT_EXTRAS).dup
end

def hands_empty?
  DRC.right_hand.nil? && DRC.left_hand.nil?
end

# The hand display and room title can lag the game text by a moment
def settle
  10.times do
    return true if yield

    pause 0.1
  end
  false
end

def in_room?(pattern)
  [XMLData.room_title, XMLData.room_name].any? { |title| title.to_s =~ pattern }
end

def in_chamber?
  in_room?(CHAMBER)
end

# Walks to the hometown's Carousel and opens your vault, starting from the
# chamber or a booth if you're in one already. Remembers how far it got in
# @vault_steps so leave_vault can undo it. Says why and returns false if it
# can't.
def open_vault(settings)
  @vault_steps = []
  if in_room?(CAROUSEL_CHAMBER)
    # Already in, maybe with the vault open ("That is already open.")
    @vault_steps.push(:booth, :chamber)
  else
    return false unless into_booth(settings)
    return false unless into_chamber
  end

  result = DRC.bput('open vault', *VAULT_OPENED, RENT_DUE, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/)
  unless VAULT_OPENED.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
    DRC.message("stash: the vault didn't open: #{result.empty? ? 'no reply' : result}")
    return false
  end
  @vault_steps << :open
  true
end

# To the hometown's Carousel and through an arch, unless you're in a booth
# already
def into_booth(settings)
  if in_room?(CAROUSEL_BOOTH)
    @vault_steps << :booth
    return true
  end

  room = get_data('town')[settings.hometown]&.dig('vault', 'id')
  unless room
    DRC.message("stash: no vault listed for your hometown, #{settings.hometown}.")
    return false
  end
  unless DRCT.walk_to(room)
    DRC.message("stash: couldn't walk to the Carousel (room #{room}).")
    return false
  end
  enter_booth
end

# From the booth through its door into the vault chamber
def into_chamber
  unless DRC.bput('pull lever', LEVER_PULLED, *NOT_FOUND, /^You can't/) =~ LEVER_PULLED
    DRC.message("stash: pulling the lever didn't open the door.")
    return false
  end

  DRC.bput('go door', /.+/)
  unless settle { in_chamber? }
    DRC.message("stash: GO DOOR didn't reach the Carousel Chamber. Room: #{XMLData.room_title.inspect}")
    return false
  end
  @vault_steps << :chamber
  true
end

# Through the first arch whose booth is free, waiting a while if all are in use
def enter_booth
  6.times do
    ARCHES.each do |arch|
      result = DRC.bput(arch, ARCH_IN, RENT_DUE, ARCH_RESTRICTED, ARCH_BUSY, *NOT_FOUND)
      if result =~ ARCH_IN
        @vault_steps << :booth
        return true
      end
      if result =~ RENT_DUE
        DRC.message('stash: vault rent is due. Pay it at the Carousel desk (GO DESK), then try again.')
        return false
      end
      # Not in the Carousel any more (say, someone went through an arch by hand)
      if NOT_FOUND.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
        DRC.message("stash: there's no #{arch.split[1]} arch here, so stopping.")
        return false
      end
    end
    DRC.message('stash: every booth is busy. Waiting 10 seconds.')
    pause 10
  end
  DRC.message('stash: gave up waiting for a free booth.')
  false
end

# Closes the vault and goes back out to the Carousel, as far as open_vault got
def leave_vault
  steps = @vault_steps.to_a
  DRC.bput('close vault', /^You close the vault/, /already closed/i, /isn't open/i, *NOT_FOUND) if steps.include?(:open)
  DRC.bput('go door', /.+/) if steps.include?(:chamber)
  DRC.bput('go arch', /door slams closed/, /.+/) if steps.include?(:booth)
  @vault_steps = []
end

# All your crafting gear, as item => the disciplines it's for, in yaml order.
# Something two disciplines use comes back with ;unstash for either one.
def crafting_gear(settings)
  tools = {
    'forging'    => settings.forging_tools.to_a,
    'shaping'    => settings.shaping_tools.to_a,
    'enchanting' => settings.enchanting_tools.to_a,
    'outfitting' => settings.outfitting_tools.to_a,
    'alchemy'    => settings.alchemy_tools.to_a
  }
  DISCIPLINES.each_with_object({}) do |discipline, gear|
    (tools[discipline] + SUPPLIES[discipline]).each { |item| gear[item] = gear.fetch(item, []) | [discipline] }
  end
end

# The part of the crafting gear these disciplines use
def gear_for(disciplines, gear)
  gear.select { |_item, used_for| (used_for & disciplines).any? }
end

# Your extras that aren't crafting gear, as item => ['extras']
def extras_for(gear)
  (load_extras - gear.keys).to_h { |item| [item, ['extras']] }
end

# The disciplines whose MATERIALS match this item name
def material_uses(name)
  DISCIPLINES.select { |discipline| MATERIALS[discipline].values.any? { |pattern| name =~ pattern } }
end

# The crafting materials these disciplines use that LOOK IN shows in your
# containers, as [what to GET, what it's for, container, name LOOK showed].
# GET only takes the one word right before the noun, so "huge pewter bar" is
# fetched as "pewter bar".
def find_materials(disciplines, settings)
  return [] if disciplines.empty?

  containers = ([settings.crafting_container] + settings.storage_containers.to_a).compact.uniq
  # A harness answers LOOK IN with "You have ... secured to your harness.",
  # which DRCI doesn't know, so it waited 15 seconds for nothing on every
  # stash (2026-11-09). Only weapons go on one.
  containers.reject! { |container| container =~ NOT_LOOKED_IN }
  containers.flat_map do |container|
    DRCI.get_item_list(container, 'look').to_a.filter_map do |name|
      used_for = material_uses(name)
      [name.split.last(2).join(' '), used_for, container, name] if (used_for & disciplines).any?
    end
  end
end

# What ;unstash asks the vault for. A bare noun gets the word before it in
# the name, so "codex" comes back as "kidskin codex" and not some other codex
# already in the vault. Not for "flask of grey oil": whether GREY OIL works
# there is unknown, so that stays OIL.
def vault_address(item, name)
  return item if item.include?(' ') || name.nil?

  words = name.split
  index = words.rindex(item)
  return item unless index&.positive? && !words[0...index].include?('of')

  adjective = words[index - 1]
  %w[a an some the].include?(adjective) ? item : "#{adjective} #{item}"
end

# The ways to try GETting a material, from the name LOOK showed. The last two
# words ("pewter bar") usually work, but not when the material's own name is
# two words: "thin Imperial weave cloth" may not answer to WEAVE CLOTH, as the
# wavy Elven gold spiral didn't answer to GOLD SPIRAL (2026-11-11). Then each
# other word with the noun ("Imperial cloth", "thin cloth"), then the noun.
def material_addresses(item, seen_as)
  words = seen_as.split
  noun = words.last
  ([item] + words[0...-1].reverse.map { |word| "#{word} #{noun}" } + [noun]).uniq
end

# A name GET gave, the way LOOK shows it, for MATERIALS to match: only deeds
# differ
def look_name(name)
  name.to_s.sub(DEED_FOR, '\2 \1 deed')
end

# Whether a name GET gave is a material these disciplines use: a looser name
# ("cloth") can pick up the chamois cloth
def stashable_material?(name, disciplines)
  (material_uses(look_name(name)) & disciplines).any?
end

# Drops what's in hand down the vault's garbage chute
def into_chute?(item)
  DRC.bput("put my #{item} in chute", *CHUTE_DROPPED, *NOT_FOUND, *PUT_FAILURE) =~ CHUTE_DROPPED.first && settle { hands_empty? }
end

# Throws out what's in hand: down the chute at the vault, else into a bin if
# the room has one, or dropped (DRCI.dispose_trash)
def throw_away?(item, store)
  return into_chute?(item) if store == :vault

  DRCI.dispose_trash(item) && settle { hands_empty? }
end

# Opens the Eddy and LOOKs in its portal, which GET needs first. False if
# you don't have one or can't reach it here.
def eddy_ready?
  opened = DRC.bput("open #{EDDY}", *EDDY_OPENED, *EDDY_UNREACHABLE)
  return false unless EDDY_OPENED.any? { |pattern| opened =~ pattern }

  looked = DRC.bput("look in #{EDDY_PORTAL}", *EDDY_LOOKED, *EDDY_UNREACHABLE)
  EDDY_LOOKED.any? { |pattern| looked =~ pattern }
end

# Puts what's in hand in the Eddy or the vault: :put, :full, or :failed. In
# the Eddy, empty hands after are what count, as its messages aren't all
# known yet.
def put_in_store(item, store)
  return put_in_vault(item) if store == :vault

  result = DRC.bput("put my #{item} in #{EDDY}", *PUT_SUCCESS, *EDDY_FULL, *EDDY_REFUSED)
  return :put if settle { hands_empty? }
  return :full if EDDY_FULL.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }

  :failed
end

# Gets the item into your hand, from the container if one is given. Returns
# the GET line, or nil if you don't have one.
def take_out(item, container)
  from = container ? " from my #{container}" : ''
  result = DRC.bput("get my #{item}#{from}", *GET_SUCCESS, *NOT_FOUND, *DRCI::GET_ITEM_FAILURE_PATTERNS)
  result if GET_SUCCESS.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern } && settle { !hands_empty? }
end

# Returns :put, :full, or :failed
def put_in_vault(item)
  result = DRC.bput("put my #{item} in vault", *PUT_SUCCESS, *VAULT_FULL, *NOT_FOUND, *PUT_FAILURE)
  return :put if PUT_SUCCESS.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern } && settle { hands_empty? }
  return :full if VAULT_FULL.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }

  :failed
end

# Back where it came from, then the crafting container, then plain STOW
def put_back(item, *places)
  return if DRCI.put_away_item?(item, places.compact.uniq + [nil])

  DRC.message("stash: couldn't put #{item} back. It's still in your hand.")
  exit
end

# gear comes out of the crafting container, one of each; extras come from
# anywhere, every one you have. Both are item => what it's for. Then every
# crafting material the material_disciplines use, from wherever it is.
def stash_items(gear, extras, settings, material_disciplines = [])
  container = settings.crafting_container
  unless hands_empty?
    DRC.message('stash: empty your hands first.')
    exit
  end

  jobs = gear.map { |item, used_for| [item, used_for, container, true] } +
         find_materials(material_disciplines, settings).map { |item, used_for, from, seen_as| [item, used_for, from, true, seen_as] } +
         extras.map { |item, used_for| [item, used_for, nil, false] }
  # ;stash materials when you carry none: no trip to the vault for nothing
  if jobs.empty?
    DRC.message('stash: nothing to stash.')
    return
  end

  stashed = load_yaml(STASHED, [])
  results = Hash.new { |hash, key| hash[key] = [] }
  taken = []

  # Into the Eddy if you have one here. What it won't take goes to the vault.
  rest = eddy_ready? ? stash_jobs(jobs, :eddy, stashed, results, taken, settings, material_disciplines) : jobs
  unless rest.empty?
    begin
      if open_vault(settings)
        stash_jobs(rest, :vault, stashed, results, taken, settings, material_disciplines)
      else
        results[:vault_shut] = rest.map(&:first)
      end
    ensure
      leave_vault
    end
  end

  DRC.message("stash: put in your Eddy: #{results[:eddy].join(', ')}") unless results[:eddy].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: the Eddy wouldn't take these, so they went to the vault: #{results[:eddy_refused].uniq.join(', ')}") unless results[:eddy_refused].empty?
  DRC.message('stash: the Eddy is full, so the rest went to the vault.') unless results[:eddy_full].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: put in your vault: #{results[:vault].join(', ')}") unless results[:vault].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: threw out: #{results[:trashed].join(', ')}") unless results[:trashed].empty?
  if %i[eddy vault trashed left_over missed failed vault_shut].all? { |key| results[key].empty? }
    DRC.message('stash: nothing to stash.')
  end
  DRC.message("stash: the vault didn't open, so these stay with you: #{results[:vault_shut].uniq.join(', ')}") unless results[:vault_shut].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: the vault is full, kept: #{results[:left_over].uniq.join(', ')}") unless results[:left_over].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: the vault wouldn't take these, kept them: #{results[:failed].join(', ')}") unless results[:failed].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: saw these but GET couldn't pick them up: #{results[:missed].join(', ')}") unless results[:missed].empty?
end

# Puts each job's things in the Eddy (store :eddy) or the vault (:vault),
# writing each down in stashed. Returns the jobs the Eddy wouldn't take, all
# of them from the first one it was full for, so they go to the vault.
def stash_jobs(jobs, store, stashed, results, taken, settings, material_disciplines)
  container = settings.crafting_container
  rest = []
  full = false
  jobs.each do |job|
    item, used_for, take_from, just_one, seen_as = job
    if full
      if store == :eddy
        rest << job
      elsif DRCI.exists?(item, take_from)
        results[:left_over] << item
      end
      next
    end

    got_any = false
    # A material that doesn't answer to its usual name gets the other
    # names to try (material_addresses); gear and extras have just the one
    addresses = seen_as ? material_addresses(item, seen_as) : [item]
    address = addresses.shift
    loop do
      line = take_out(address, take_from)
      unless line
        break if got_any || addresses.empty?

        address = addresses.shift
        next
      end
      from = line[GET_SOURCE, 1] || take_from
      name = line[GET_NAME, 1]
      if seen_as && !stashable_material?(name, material_disciplines)
        put_back(address, from, container)
        break
      end
      got_any = true
      # Coal nuggets are thrown out, not stashed or listed
      if seen_as && name =~ TRASH_PATTERN
        unless throw_away?(address, store)
          results[:failed] << name
          put_back(address, from, container)
          break
        end
        results[:trashed] << name
        taken << name.to_s.downcase
        next
      end
      case put_in_store(address, store)
      when :put
        results[store] << (seen_as && name ? name : address)
        taken << look_name(name).downcase
        # A copy of used_for each time: two codices sharing one array would
        # be written as a YAML alias, which safe_load refuses to read back.
        # A material is for what its own name says, and ;unstash asks for it
        # by its own last two words first ("titanese cloth", not the "thin
        # cloth" that found it), as a looser name may have found another one.
        uses = seen_as ? material_uses(look_name(name)) : used_for.dup
        address_for_unstash = seen_as && name ? look_name(name).split.last(2).join(' ') : vault_address(address, name)
        entry = { 'item' => address_for_unstash, 'name' => name, 'from' => from, 'for' => uses }
        # ;unstash crafting leaves these stashed; ;unstash materials gets them
        entry['kind'] = 'materials' if seen_as
        entry['in'] = 'eddy' if store == :eddy
        stashed << entry
        save_yaml(STASHED, stashed)
        break if just_one
      when :full
        full = true
        put_back(address, from, container)
        if store == :eddy
          results[:eddy_full] << address
          rest << job
        else
          results[:left_over] << address
        end
        break
      else
        put_back(address, from, container)
        if store == :eddy
          results[:eddy_refused] << (name || address)
          rest << job
        else
          results[:failed] << (name || address)
        end
        break
      end
    end
    # One GET can take several things LOOK listed apart ("electroweave
    # cloth" takes the thin and thick ones too), so only one that nothing
    # took is a miss
    results[:missed] << "#{seen_as} (#{take_from})" if seen_as && !got_any && !taken.include?(seen_as.downcase)
  end
  rest
end

# The weapons in your yaml's weapon_training, each once (the gilt dagger is
# both Small Edged and Offhand Weapon), as [weapon_training name, gear item].
# One that isn't in your yaml's gear list is left out: EquipmentManager only
# knows where gear-list things are kept.
def weapons_to_stash(settings, manager)
  settings.weapon_training.to_h.values.compact.uniq.filter_map do |description|
    weapon = manager.item_by_desc(description)
    DRC.message("stash: #{description} isn't in your yaml's gear list, so it stays where it is.") unless weapon
    [description, weapon] if weapon
  end
end

# Puts a weapon in hand back where it's kept, as after a hunt: worn again if
# your standard gear set wears it, else on its harness, in its container,
# or STOWed (into the sheath, for the cutlass and broadsword)
def return_weapon(manager)
  return if manager.return_held_gear && settle { hands_empty? }

  DRC.message("stash: couldn't put #{DRC.right_hand || DRC.left_hand} back. It's still in your hand.")
  exit
end

# ;stash weapons, for when you're not hunting. Each weapon comes out of
# wherever it's kept, the way combat-trainer gets it: taken off if you wear
# it (the voulge, the knuckles), off its harness (the throwing club, the
# staff), out of its sheath or container. They go in the Eddy, or the vault
# for what the Eddy won't take. ;unstash weapons puts each back the same way
# combat-trainer does after a hunt, and t2's hunt block runs it first.
def stash_weapons(settings)
  unless hands_empty?
    DRC.message('stash: empty your hands first.')
    exit
  end

  manager = EquipmentManager.new(settings)
  weapons = weapons_to_stash(settings, manager)
  if weapons.empty?
    DRC.message('stash: no weapons to stash: your yaml has none in weapon_training.')
    return
  end

  stashed = load_yaml(STASHED, [])
  results = Hash.new { |hash, key| hash[key] = [] }

  eddy = eddy_ready?
  rest = eddy ? weapons_into(weapons, :eddy, manager, stashed, results) : weapons
  eddy_left = rest.map(&:first)
  unless rest.empty?
    begin
      if open_vault(settings)
        results[:kept] = weapons_into(rest, :vault, manager, stashed, results).map(&:first)
      else
        results[:vault_shut] = rest.map(&:first)
      end
    ensure
      leave_vault
    end
  end

  DRC.message("stash: put in your Eddy: #{results[:eddy].join(', ')}") unless results[:eddy].empty?
  if eddy && !eddy_left.empty?
    DRC.message("stash: #{results[:eddy_full].empty? ? "the Eddy wouldn't take these" : 'the Eddy is full, so it didn\'t take these'}: #{eddy_left.join(', ')}")
  end
  DRC.message("stash: put in your vault: #{results[:vault].join(', ')}") unless results[:vault].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: #{results[:vault_full].empty? ? "the vault wouldn't take these" : 'the vault is full'}, kept them: #{results[:kept].join(', ')}") unless results[:kept].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: the vault didn't open, so these stay with you: #{results[:vault_shut].join(', ')}") unless results[:vault_shut].empty?
  DRC.message("stash: couldn't find these to stash: #{results[:not_found].join(', ')}") unless results[:not_found].empty?
  DRC.message('stash: ;unstash weapons gets them back before you hunt.') unless results[:eddy].empty? && results[:vault].empty?
end

# Puts each weapon in the Eddy (store :eddy) or the vault, writing it down.
# One the store won't take goes back where it's kept, and it and the rest
# are returned, all of them from the first one the store was full for.
def weapons_into(weapons, store, manager, stashed, results)
  rest = []
  full = false
  weapons.each do |description, weapon|
    if full
      rest << [description, weapon]
      next
    end
    unless manager.get_item?(weapon) && settle { !hands_empty? }
      results[:not_found] << description
      next
    end

    result = put_in_store(weapon.short_name, store)
    if result == :put
      results[store] << description
      # No name: the GET line gives the full description, which the yaml
      # doesn't have, so ;unstash takes the weapon by short_name without
      # checking it
      entry = { 'item' => weapon.short_name, 'name' => nil, 'from' => 'gear', 'for' => ['weapons'] }
      entry['in'] = 'eddy' if store == :eddy
      stashed << entry
      save_yaml(STASHED, stashed)
    else
      if result == :full
        full = true
        results[:"#{store}_full"] << description
      end
      rest << [description, weapon]
      return_weapon(manager)
    end
  end
  rest
end

def add_extra(item)
  if item.empty?
    DRC.message('stash: add what? For example: ;stash add gem pouch')
    return
  end

  extras = load_extras
  if extras.include?(item)
    DRC.message("stash: #{item} is already on your extras.")
    return
  end

  result = DRC.bput("tap my #{item}", *TAP_SUCCESS, *NOT_FOUND)
  unless TAP_SUCCESS.any? { |pattern| result =~ pattern }
    DRC.message("stash: TAP couldn't find a \"#{item}\" on you, so it's not added. Check the name and try again.")
    return
  end

  name, container, state = result.match(TAP_NAME)&.captures
  if state == 'wearing'
    DRC.message("stash: you're wearing the #{name}. Stash only takes things you carry, so it's not added.")
    return
  end

  extras << item
  save_yaml(EXTRAS, extras)
  where = if container then ", in your #{container}"
          elsif state then ", that you're #{state}"
          end
  DRC.message("stash: added #{item} (#{name || result}#{where}). ;stash extras or ;stash all will stash every one you have.")
end

def remove_extra(item)
  extras = load_extras
  if extras.delete(item)
    save_yaml(EXTRAS, extras)
    DRC.message("stash: removed #{item}. Extras now: #{extras.empty? ? 'none' : extras.join(', ')}")
  else
    DRC.message("stash: #{item.empty? ? 'remove what?' : "#{item} isn't on your extras."} Extras: #{extras.join(', ')}")
  end
end

def show_list(gear, settings)
  DISCIPLINES.each do |discipline|
    tools = gear_for([discipline], gear).keys
    materials = MATERIALS[discipline].keys
    DRC.message("stash: #{discipline} (;stash #{discipline}): #{tools.empty? ? 'no gear' : tools.join(', ')}" \
                "#{", plus any #{materials.join(', ')}" unless materials.empty?}")
  end
  DRC.message("stash: thrown out instead of stashed: #{TRASH.join(', ')}")
  weapons = settings.weapon_training.to_h.values.compact.uniq
  DRC.message("stash: weapons (;stash weapons): #{weapons.empty? ? 'none' : weapons.join(', ')}")
  extras = load_extras
  DRC.message("stash: extras (;stash extras): #{extras.empty? ? 'none' : extras.join(', ')}")

  stashed = load_yaml(STASHED, [])
  if stashed.empty?
    DRC.message('stash: nothing is stashed right now.')
    return
  end

  stashed.group_by { |entry| [entry['in'], entry['for'].to_a.join('/'), entry['kind']] }.each do |(store, used_for, kind), entries|
    names = entries.map { |entry| entry['name'] || entry['item'] }
    what = [kind, ("for #{used_for}" unless used_for.empty?)].compact.join(' ')
    DRC.message("stash: in your #{store == 'eddy' ? 'Eddy' : 'vault'}#{" (#{what})" unless what.empty?}: #{names.join(', ')}")
  end
  DRC.message('stash: ;unstash gets it all back. ;unstash forging, shaping, enchanting, outfitting, alchemy, crafting, weapons or extras ' \
              'gets just that, without materials (;unstash crafting forging is the same as ;unstash forging); ' \
              ';unstash materials (or ;unstash materials forging) gets the materials.')
end

settings = get_settings
command = Script.current.vars[1].to_s.downcase
item = Script.current.vars[2..].to_a.compact.join(' ').downcase.strip
gear = crafting_gear(settings)

case command
when 'crafting'
  if item.empty?
    stash_items(gear, {}, settings, DISCIPLINES)
  # One discipline, the same as ;stash <discipline>: t2's crafting blocks
  # start with ;unstash crafting <discipline> and end with this
  elsif DISCIPLINES.include?(item)
    stash_items(gear_for([item], gear), {}, settings, [item])
  else
    DRC.message("stash: use ;stash crafting, or ;stash crafting #{DISCIPLINES.join(', ')}.")
  end
when *DISCIPLINES
  stash_items(gear_for([command], gear), {}, settings, [command])
when 'materials', 'material'
  # Just the materials, the heavy part, leaving the tools where they are
  if item.empty?
    stash_items({}, {}, settings, DISCIPLINES)
  elsif DISCIPLINES.include?(item) && !MATERIALS[item].empty?
    stash_items({}, {}, settings, [item])
  else
    DRC.message("stash: #{item} has no materials. Use ;stash materials, or ;stash materials #{DISCIPLINES.reject { |discipline| MATERIALS[discipline].empty? }.join(', ')}.")
  end
when 'weapons', 'weapon'
  stash_weapons(settings)
when 'extras'
  stash_items({}, extras_for(gear), settings)
when 'all'
  stash_items(gear, extras_for(gear), settings, DISCIPLINES)
when 'add'
  add_extra(item)
when 'remove'
  remove_extra(item)
when 'list'
  show_list(gear, settings)
else
  DRC.message('stash: use ;stash crafting, forging, shaping, enchanting, outfitting, alchemy, materials, weapons, extras, all, add <item>, remove <item>, or list.')
end
